Package: jellyqda
Type: Package
Title: RStudio-Native, Fully Offline Coding of Interview Transcripts
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Shelly", email = "shelly@example.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: jellyqda is a small, RStudio-native tool for qualitative coding of
    interview transcripts (and field notes) that works completely offline. All
    project data lives in a single SQLite file (one '.jellyqda' file per
    project); imported text is frozen at import time so character offsets
    never drift. Coding happens through a narrow, scriptable API that returns
    tibbles: qda_open(), qda_import(), qda_sources(), qda_view(), qda_codes(),
    qda_code_add(), qda_code(), qda_segments(), qda_export(), qda_backup() and
    qda_stats(). Every action is recorded in an audit trail (events table) that
    can be exported for the methods section of a thesis. No network access is
    ever required or attempted.
